{
  "sn35.93:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.93 ",
  "sn35.93:0.2": "9. With Channa ",
  "sn35.93:0.3": "A Duality (2nd) ",
  "sn35.93:1.1": "“Mendicants, consciousness originates dependent on a duality. ",
  "sn35.93:1.2": "And what is that duality? ",
  "sn35.93:1.3": "Eye consciousness arises dependent on the eye and sights. ",
  "sn35.93:1.4": "The eye is impermanent, decaying, and perishing. ",
  "sn35.93:1.5": "Sights are impermanent, decaying, and perishing. ",
  "sn35.93:1.6": "So this duality is tottering and toppling; it’s impermanent, decaying, and perishing. ",
  "sn35.93:1.7": "Eye consciousness is impermanent, decaying, and perishing. ",
  "sn35.93:1.8": "And the causes and reasons that give rise to eye consciousness are also impermanent, decaying, and perishing. ",
  "sn35.93:1.9": "But since eye consciousness has arisen dependent on conditions that are impermanent, how could it be permanent? ",
  "sn35.93:1.10": "The meeting, coming together, and joining together of these three things is called eye contact. ",
  "sn35.93:1.11": "Eye contact is also impermanent, decaying, and perishing. ",
  "sn35.93:1.12": "And the causes and reasons that give rise to eye contact are also impermanent, decaying, and perishing. ",
  "sn35.93:1.13": "But since eye contact has arisen dependent on conditions that are impermanent, how could it be permanent? ",
  "sn35.93:1.14": "Contacted one feels; contacted one intends; contacted one perceives. ",
  "sn35.93:1.15": "So these things too are tottering and toppling; th